## Analysis

The baseline uses a **64-point full-wave LUT with nearest-neighbor sampling**. The top 6 bits of the phase (`phase[15:10]`) select a table entry, and the remaining **10 bits of sub-bin phase information are simply discarded**. This is the dominant source of error — it caps SQNR at ~25 dB.

The fix with the best precision-per-area tradeoff is **linear interpolation**: use the low phase bits as a fractional weight between adjacent table entries. This recovers sub-bin resolution and pushes SQNR toward the interpolation residual limit (~60 dB), at the cost of a single small `16×8` signed multiplier that runs combinationally in the same pipeline stage (no throughput penalty).

